[{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>For each of the following statements, write the negation:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>The cat is black.</p></li><li><p>Some cats are black.</p></li><li><p>Some cats are not black.</p></li><li><p>Line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is parallel to line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>The probability has increased.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even and prime.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>The cat is not black</p></li><li><p>No cats are black</p></li><li><p>All cats are black</p></li><li><p>Line A is not parallel to line B</p></li><li><p>The probability has not increased</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\ne2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd and not prime</p></li></ol>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>For each of the following statements, write the negation:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>For all integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, either <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is positive or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is negative.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a number with at least 3 distinct prime factors.</p></li><li><p>Every prime number is odd.</p></li><li><p>The sum of a rational number and an irrational number is always irrational.</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>There exists an integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> that is neither positive nor negative (e.g. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>)</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a number with less than 3 distinct prime factors</p></li><li><p>There exists at least one prime number that is not odd (e.g. 2)</p></li><li><p>There exists a rational number and an irrational number whose sum is rational.</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd</p></li></ol>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>A student is attempting to prove by contradiction that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac pq+\\frac qp\\geq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Their first line of working states:</p><blockquote><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are negative numbers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac pq+\\frac qp\\geq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></blockquote><p>Correct their first line.</p>","steps":["<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac pq+\\frac qp&lt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Prove that the following numbers are irrational:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<p><strong>a)</strong> Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2=\\frac{a^2}{b^2}\\Rightarrow a^2=2b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k)^2=4k^2=2b^2\\Rightarrow 2k^2=b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even. This contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>","<p><strong>b)</strong> Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3=\\frac{a^2}{b^2}\\Rightarrow a^2=3b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3k)^2=9k^2=3b^2\\Rightarrow 3k^2=b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3. This contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>","<p><strong>c)</strong> Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5=\\frac{a^2}{b^2}\\Rightarrow a^2=5b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5k)^2=25k^2=5b^2\\Rightarrow5k^2=b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5. This contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an irrational number.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]5=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5=\\frac{a^3}{b^3}\\Rightarrow a^3=5b^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(5k)^3=125k^3=5b^3\\Rightarrow125k^3=b^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5. This contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rational, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\sqrt2=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2=\\frac ab-1\\Rightarrow\\sqrt2=\\frac{a-b}{b}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2=\\left(\\frac{a-b}{b}\\right)^2\\Rightarrow(a-b)^2=2b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(a-b)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a-b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a-b=2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k)^2=4k^2=2b^2\\Rightarrow2k^2=b^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even. This contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Prove that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-5x+6&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2&lt;x&lt;3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Assume that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-5x+6&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\leq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2-5x+6=(x-2)(x-3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So we are assuming that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x-2)(x-3)&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. This has solutions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2&lt;x&lt;3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which contradicts <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\leq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-5x+6&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2&lt;x&lt;3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Prove that there is no greatest multiple of 3</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that there is a greatest multiple of 3, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(k+1)=3k+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is both a multiple of 3 and greater than <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which contradicts the assumption. Therefore there is no greatest multiple of 3.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Prove that there are infinitely many prime numbers.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that there is a largest prime number, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N=p_1p_2\\ldots p_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p_1,p_2,\\ldots,p_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are all the prime numbers. Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N+1=p_1p_2\\ldots p_n+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is either prime or has a prime factor not in the list, which is a contradiction. Therefore there are infinitely many prime numbers.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Prove that the difference between a rational number and an irrational number is always irrational.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that the difference between a rational number and an irrational number is rational. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be integers. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be rational (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be irrational. So assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab-c=\\frac pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"c=\\frac ab-\\frac pq=\\frac{aq}{bq}-\\frac{bp}{bq}=\\frac{aq-bp}{bq}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which contradicts <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> being irrational. Therefore the difference between a rational number and an irrational number is always irrational.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q11","number":11,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Prove that the product of a positive rational number and a positive irrational number is irrational</p></li><li><p>Hence, state the values for which it is not true that the product of a rational and an irrational number is irrational.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<p><strong>a)</strong> Assume that the product of a rational number and an irrational number is rational. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be integers. Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be rational (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be irrational. So assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\\times c=\\frac pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"c=\\frac pq\\div\\frac ab=\\frac pq\\times\\frac ba=\\frac{bp}{aq}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which contradicts <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> being irrational. Therefore the product of a positive rational and a positive irrational number is irrational.</p>","<p><strong>b)</strong> It is true for all cases except 0.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Lynn has sketched the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=kx^2-3kx+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which can be seen below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.44/questions/assets/diagrams/244-q12.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>She claims that the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which this is the correct sketch are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;k&lt;\\frac{32}{9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Use proof by contradiction to prove her claim.</p>","steps":["<p>There are no real solutions when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(-3k)^2-4k\\times8&lt;0\\Rightarrow9k^2-32k&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Assume that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9k^2-32k&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\leq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\geq\\frac{32}{9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k\\leq0\\text{ or }k\\geq\\frac{32}{9}\\Rightarrow k(9k-32)\\geq0\\Rightarrow9k^2-32k\\geq0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9k^2-32k&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kx^2-3kx+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has no real roots, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9k^2-32k&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;k&lt;\\frac{32}{9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Prove that for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+\\frac1x\\geq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Assume that for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+\\frac1x&lt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}{x}+\\frac1x&lt;2\\Rightarrow\\frac{x^2+1}{x}&lt;2\\Rightarrow x^2+1&lt;2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2-2x+1&lt;0\\Rightarrow(x-1)^2&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But anything squared is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so this is a contradiction. Therefore for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+\\frac1x\\geq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Prove that for any real value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2+b^2&gt;2ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Assume that for any value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2+b^2&lt;2ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a^2-2ab+b^2&lt;0\\Rightarrow(a-b)(a-b)&lt;0\\Rightarrow(a-b)^2&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But anything squared is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so this is a contradiction. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2+b^2\\geq2ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an irrational number.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a rational number. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is non-zero, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is in its simplified form.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3=\\frac ab\\Rightarrow3=10^{a/b}\\Rightarrow3^b=(10^{a/b})^b=10^a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But powers of 3 are odd and powers of 10 are even, therefore this contradicts <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3=\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is irrational.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q16","number":16,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p^2-6q=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd</p></li><li><p>Hence, prove by contradiction that there are no integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2-6b=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<p><strong>a)</strong> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p^2-6q=5\\Rightarrow p^2=6q+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, 5 is odd, even + odd is odd. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd.</p>","<p><strong>b)</strong> Assume integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> exist such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2-6b=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. From part a) we have that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k+1)^2-6b=5\\Rightarrow4k^2+4k+1=6b+5\\Rightarrow4k^2+4k-4=6b\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2k^2+2k-2-3b=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>There must exist a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k^2+2k-2-3b=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2k^2+2k-(2+3b)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{4+8(2+3b)}}4=-\\frac12\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{5-6b}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{5-6b}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must exist and be an integer. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-6b&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-6b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be an integer.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5-6b&gt;0\\Rightarrow b&lt;\\frac56\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer, there are no possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-6b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive integer, which contradicts the statement that integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> exist such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2-6b=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore there are no integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2-6b=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Prove that 3 is the only prime number which is 1 less than a square number.</p>","steps":["<p>Assume that there exists a prime number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is 1 less than a square number and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\ne3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=n^2-1\\text{ where }p\\ne3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=(n+1)(n-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is prime and must have precisely two factors, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=1\\times(n-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=(n+1)\\times1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Either <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n+1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n-1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Case 1: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n+1=1\\Rightarrow n=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is not a prime.</p>","<p>Case 2: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n-1=1\\Rightarrow n=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=4-1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which contradicts that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\ne3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore 3 is the only prime number which is 1 less than a square number.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.44-q18","number":18,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q18: Double Angle Formula</strong> Prove that for all real <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta\\leq\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta&gt;\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta)^2 &gt;2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\cos^2\\theta+2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta &gt;2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta+1 &gt;2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta &gt;1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin2\\theta &gt;1\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq\\sin2\\theta\\leq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a contradiction. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta\\leq\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]